  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transformative Education for sustainable development health &amp; global citizenship</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To cultivate a transformative educational landscape across seven key Asian countries (covered by the office), so that learners of all ages are healthy, happy, better able to care for one another and the planet, and to create more peaceful, just, and sustainable societies.

This initiative supports national education systems in mainstreaming Education for Sustainable Development (ESD), Global Citizenship Education (GCED), and Education for Health and Well-being (HWB) in 7 countries in Asia covered by UNESCO BGK. Activities include policy and curriculum review and formulation, capacity building for policymakers, educators, and youth, setting standards, monitoring progress, and generating knowledge on ESD and GCED. It also focuses on enhancing educational environments for safe, inclusive, gender-equitable, and health-promoting learning, alongside promoting teachers&apos; development in delivering Comprehensive Sexuality Education (CSE) to foster healthy lifestyles and respectful relationships among learners.</narrative>
  </description>
